%% generated by make_ol.py from src/T5.txt; edit the source, not this file

1. The World Economic Forum's Global Gender Gap Index began in:
(A) 1995  (B) 2006  (C) 2010  (D) 2015
Ans: ^^Answer: (B) 2006^^ — 2006, when Pakistan ranked 112th of 115.

2. Which of the following is NOT a sub-index of the Global Gender Gap Index?
(A) Economic participation  (B) Health and survival  (C) Political empowerment  (D) Access to justice
Ans: ^^Answer: (D) Access to justice^^ — The four: economic participation, educational attainment, health and survival, political empowerment.

3. In the Global Gender Gap Report 2017 Pakistan ranked:
(A) 143rd of 144  (B) 112th of 115  (C) 148th of 148  (D) None of these
Ans: ^^Answer: (A) 143rd of 144^^ — 143rd of 144 — "second-worst".

4. In the Global Gender Gap Report 2025 Pakistan ranked:
(A) 142nd of 146  (B) 143rd of 145  (C) 148th of 148  (D) 145th of 148
Ans: ^^Answer: (C) 148th of 148^^ — Last, 148th of 148, with 56.7% of the gap closed.

5. On which sub-index did Pakistan rank lowest in 2026?
(A) Economic participation  (B) Educational attainment  (C) Political empowerment  (D) None of these
Ans: ^^Answer: (A) Economic participation^^ — 144th on economic participation (130th education, 107th political empowerment).

6. Pakistan's maternal mortality ratio in the Pakistan Maternal Mortality Survey 2019 was:
(A) 70  (B) 140  (C) 186  (D) 276
Ans: ^^Answer: (C) 186^^ — 186 per 100,000 live births.

7. SDG target 3.1 aims to bring the global maternal mortality ratio below:
(A) 50  (B) 70  (C) 100  (D) 186
Ans: ^^Answer: (B) 70^^ — Below 70 per 100,000 live births by 2030.

8. "Why did Mrs X die?" was asked at the Safe Motherhood Conference, Nairobi (1987), by:
(A) Amartya Sen  (B) Mahbub ul Haq  (C) Thaddeus and Maine  (D) Mahmoud Fathalla
Ans: ^^Answer: (D) Mahmoud Fathalla^^ — Mahmoud Fathalla.

9. The "three delays" model of maternal death was described by:
(A) Thaddeus and Maine  (B) Chant and Sweetman  (C) Childs and Krook  (D) None of these
Ans: ^^Answer: (A) Thaddeus and Maine^^ — Sereen Thaddeus and Deborah Maine (1994).

10. The three delays are in deciding to seek care, reaching care and:
(A) Receiving care  (B) Paying for care  (C) Registering the birth  (D) None of these
Ans: ^^Answer: (A) Receiving care^^ — Receiving adequate care at the facility.

11. About what share of Pakistani women of reproductive age were anaemic (NNS 2018)?
(A) 22%  (B) 32%  (C) 42%  (D) 62%
Ans: ^^Answer: (C) 42%^^ — About 42%.

12. The Lady Health Worker Programme began in 1994 under:
(A) Nawaz Sharif  (B) Zia-ul-Haq  (C) Pervez Musharraf  (D) Benazir Bhutto
Ans: ^^Answer: (D) Benazir Bhutto^^ — Benazir Bhutto.

13. After the 18th Amendment (2010), health became:
(A) A federal subject  (B) A provincial subject  (C) A concurrent subject  (D) None of these
Ans: ^^Answer: (B) A provincial subject^^ — A provincial subject.

14. Article 25A requires free and compulsory education for children aged:
(A) 3 to 14  (B) 5 to 16  (C) 6 to 18  (D) 5 to 18
Ans: ^^Answer: (B) 5 to 16^^ — Ages 5 to 16 (18th Amendment, 2010).

15. Pakistan's literacy rate in the Census 2023 was about:
(A) 48%  (B) 58%  (C) 60.65%  (D) 68%
Ans: ^^Answer: (C) 60.65%^^ — 60.65% — about 68% for men and 53% for women.

16. The province with the lowest female literacy in Pakistan is:
(A) Sindh  (B) Khyber Pakhtunkhwa  (C) Punjab  (D) Balochistan
Ans: ^^Answer: (D) Balochistan^^ — Balochistan.

17. Female labour-force participation in Pakistan in the Labour Force Survey 2024–25 was:
(A) 14.5%  (B) 21.4%  (C) 24.4%  (D) 33.8%
Ans: ^^Answer: (C) 24.4%^^ — 24.4% (21.4% in 2020–21).

18. The "second shift" (1989) — women's unpaid work after paid work — was named by:
(A) Marilyn Waring  (B) Diane Elson  (C) Guy Standing  (D) Arlie Hochschild
Ans: ^^Answer: (D) Arlie Hochschild^^ — Arlie Hochschild.

19. The first Home-Based Workers Act in Pakistan was passed in 2018 by:
(A) Punjab  (B) Khyber Pakhtunkhwa  (C) Balochistan  (D) None of these
Ans: ^^Answer: (D) None of these^^ — None of these — Sindh (2018); Punjab passed a Domestic Workers Act in 2019.

20. The federal Maternity and Paternity Leave Act was passed in:
(A) 2010  (B) 2016  (C) 2020  (D) 2022
Ans: ^^Answer: (C) 2020^^ — 2020.

21. Which Article of the Constitution calls for the full participation of women in all spheres of national life?
(A) Article 25  (B) Article 32  (C) Article 34  (D) Article 35
Ans: ^^Answer: (C) Article 34^^ — Article 34 (Art. 25 equality; Art. 32 local government; Art. 35 family).

22. Which is correct about the Constitution of 1973?
(A) Article 25 allows special provision for women  (B) Article 34 calls for women's full participation in national life  (C) Both A and B  (D) None of these
Ans: ^^Answer: (C) Both A and B^^ — Both: Art. 25(3) allows special provision; Art. 34 requires full participation.

23. Under the MFLO 1961, a second marriage requires the permission of the:
(A) Arbitration Council  (B) Family Court  (C) Union Council chairman alone  (D) None of these
Ans: ^^Answer: (A) Arbitration Council^^ — The Arbitration Council.

24. Under the MFLO, a *talaq* takes effect after notice to the Union Council of:
(A) 30 days  (B) 60 days  (C) 90 days  (D) 120 days
Ans: ^^Answer: (C) 90 days^^ — 90 days.

25. A wife's right to *khula* was recognised in:
(A) *Saima Waheed* (2004)  (B) *Khurshid Bibi v. Muhammad Amin* (1967)  (C) *Shah Bano* (1985)  (D) None of these
Ans: ^^Answer: (B) *Khurshid Bibi v. Muhammad Amin* (1967)^^ — *Khurshid Bibi v. Muhammad Amin* (1967).

26. The Dissolution of Muslim Marriages Act was passed in:
(A) 1929  (B) 1939  (C) 1961  (D) 1964
Ans: ^^Answer: (B) 1939^^ — 1939.

27. The first law in Pakistan to set 18 as the minimum marriage age for girls was passed by:
(A) Sindh, 2013  (B) Punjab, 2015  (C) Islamabad, 2025  (D) None of these
Ans: ^^Answer: (A) Sindh, 2013^^ — Sindh Child Marriages Restraint Act 2013; Islamabad followed in 2025.

28. The Prevention of Anti-Women Practices Act 2011 criminalised all of the following EXCEPT:
(A) Forced marriage  (B) *Vani*/*swara*  (C) Denial of inheritance  (D) Dowry
Ans: ^^Answer: (D) Dowry^^ — Dowry is governed by the Dowry and Bridal Gifts (Restriction) Act 1976.

29. The Enforcement of Women's Property Rights Act (Islamabad) was passed in:
(A) 2011  (B) 2016  (C) 2020  (D) 2021
Ans: ^^Answer: (C) 2020^^ — 2020.

30. Pakistan's mobile-internet gender gap (GSMA, 2024–25) fell from 38% to:
(A) 8%  (B) 25%  (C) 30%  (D) None of these
Ans: ^^Answer: (B) 25%^^ — 25%.

31. The term "matrix of domination" (1990) was introduced by:
(A) Kimberlé Crenshaw  (B) Patricia Hill Collins  (C) bell hooks  (D) Audre Lorde
Ans: ^^Answer: (B) Patricia Hill Collins^^ — Patricia Hill Collins.

32. Pakistan ratified the Convention on the Rights of Persons with Disabilities in:
(A) 1981  (B) 2008  (C) 2011  (D) 2018
Ans: ^^Answer: (C) 2011^^ — 2011.

33. The Benazir Income Support Programme (2008) pays cash to:
(A) Women  (B) Male heads of household  (C) Children directly  (D) None of these
Ans: ^^Answer: (A) Women^^ — Women.
